proof.text:
On the raw localized Hom modules define $F_E(u\otimes e)=F(u)\otimes e$ and $F_E(K)=F(K)$. By $R$-linearity of $F$ (Step 3) and module base change, it is a well-defined $E$-linear Hom map: $F(ru)\otimes e=rF(u)\otimes e=F(u)\otimes re$. For pure tensors,
$F_E((v\otimes b)(u\otimes a))=F(vu)\otimes ba=(F(v)\otimes b)(F(u)\otimes a)$;
bilinearity gives the law for sums, and $F_E(1\otimes1)=1\otimes1$, so $F_E$ is a functor. This is the unique $E$-linear extension, since $u\otimes e=e(u\otimes1)$.
